# routine — record, then replay
#
# The full round trip of the routine system, which nothing else covered: a routine is recorded by
# playing, the player leaves and comes back, and the routine replays on arrival into the sub-phase it
# ended on. Both halves are in one script because the replay needs a routine, and recording one is
# most of the work.
#
# WHAT IS RECORDED. The routine is [move, propose_to_buy], which is the shape a real one takes: a
# repositioning step only extends the prefix (walking somewhere is how you get somewhere, not what
# you went to do), and the first non-repositioning step is the terminus that emits the routine. So
# the walk into the wood is IN the routine but is not a routine of its own.
#
# WHAT THE REPLAY MUST GET RIGHT. Replay walks the steps headlessly and hands the game a phase
# transition. That transition has to carry BOTH where and when the replay ended — the trade menu is
# opened from a rebuilt scene, and the rebuild starts at the location's default opening area (Test
# Yard). The three routine bridges used to carry the period alone, so leaving the trade menu put the
# player back in the yard instead of the wood the routine had walked into. `expect-state where Test
# Wood` at the end is that bug, and it is the whole reason this script exists.
#
# THE SETUP. The farmer sells crops and roams: at noon she is in Test Wood, which is one plain path
# from Test Yard — the only seller in the location reachable without unlocking a door.
# --npc-affinity is what makes propose_to_buy possible at all (TradeGate wants an acquaintance).
# --observe-only pins the FIRST phase, in the yard, on the wood; the `observe` command pins the
# second, in the wood, on the farmer — a flag cannot do that, because the second phase is generated
# mid-run.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --npc-affinity CloseFriend --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon --observe-only "Test Wood"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
strategy succeed

# --- step 1: walk into the wood (a prefix step, not a routine of its own) ------
goal move
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# Pinned BEFORE the footer press: that press closes the segment and generates the next phase's
# observation, so a filter set after it would arrive too late to steer anything.
observe farmer
goal propose_to_buy
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
expect-state where Test Wood

# --- step 2: the trade, which is the terminus that emits the routine ----------
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# The recorder's rule, asserted by verb ids rather than by the routine's name: the name is built
# from the NPC's rolled name and is content, free to change.
inspect routines
expect-state routines verbs=[move,propose_to_buy]

# --- leave, go elsewhere, and come back on the routine ------------------------
# `travel neighbour` and `travel back` exist because a script cannot name either vertex: the one it
# started on is whatever the seed put under the avatar, and `travel <name>` prefers the vertex
# underfoot, which would walk straight back into the location it is trying to leave.
observe none
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

# And exactly one routine, not two. The move was consumed by the trade's emission, so the prefix has
# nothing new to say and the end-of-session pass must not emit it a second time as a bare "go to the
# wood". The complementary case — a walk that NO emission claimed — is routine_movement_only.cli.
expect-no-state routines steps=1

travel neighbour
travel-go
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

travel back
routines
routines 0
wait mode WorldView 150

# CONTINUE on the outcome box applies the phase the routine ended on. For a trade terminus that is
# the trade menu itself — reached without the walk and without the conversation, which is what a
# routine is for.
routines continue
wait mode Trading 60

# And the point of the whole script: the replay resumed in the area it ended in, not the one the
# rebuilt scene opens at.
expect-state where Test Wood
quit
